Rule: In body text and headings, number or date spans should be written using words — "from … to" or "between … and" — rather than an en dash (–). En dashes for spans are acceptable only in financial year headings, titles, terms of office, lifespans, technical content with many ranges, or limited-space contexts such as tables, lists, and social media. A violation is an en dash used to represent a span in plain body text or a heading where words would fit.

